{
  "_comment": [
    "Miami-Dade high school CAP (College Assistance Program) advisor pages.",
    "This is the core of the counselor-page strategy: every MDCPS senior high has a",
    "full-time CAP advisor who publishes a scholarship bulletin, and Miami-Dade",
    "schools run INDEPENDENT vanity domains rather than dadeschools.net subdomains,",
    "so district robots policy governs almost none of them.",
    "",
    "Two CMS patterns dominate: WordPress vanity domains with /cap/, /cap-corner/,",
    "/cap-advisor/ style slugs, and Edlio sites with /apps/pages/index.jsp?uREC_ID=.",
    "The WordPress slugs are worth brute-forcing against any MDCPS vanity domain to",
    "widen coverage later.",
    "",
    "All URLs appeared verbatim in search results; none were pattern-guessed. None",
    "are load-verified -- this harvest is the verification."
  ],
